WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.902
-Our first guest tonight
is an Academy Award-nominated

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.538
and Emmy-winning actor who you
know from shows like "Cheers"

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:09.041
and "True Detective" and films
such as "White Men Can't Jump,"

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.244
and "Zombieland,"
and "Triangle of Sadness."

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.581
He stars in "Champions," which
opens in theaters March 10th.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.581
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.650
-My name is Marcus Marakovich

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.785
and I am going to be
your basketball coach

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:21.120
for the next three months.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.490
-Nope.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.525
-Wait. What?

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.259
-I said nope.

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:31.998
[ Basketball dribbling ]

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.134
-Is this something
he normally does?

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.234
-Nope.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:39.672
-That's Darius.
He's our best player.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:44.010
I'm Johnny. I'm your homie
with an extra chromie.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.244
-Whoa.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.546
-Please welcome back to
the show, our friend,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.281
Woody Harrelson, everybody.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:51.284
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.284 --> 00:01:08.134 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.702
Welcome back.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.772
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.475
-Listen, I know you guys
are here to see Niall,

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:17.710
but I appreciate that.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.979
-Very nice of them.
Very nice of them.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.247
How do you think I -
-I'm happy to see Niall, too.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.248
-Yeah.
-Like, I saw him backstage.

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:26.685
I was, like, fawning like
a little school girl. Any way.

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:28.654
-That's very nice that
you can be honest about that.

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:29.955
-Yeah.
-I felt the same way.

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.557
I saw Niall backstage
and I had the same reaction.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:35.861
-But yeah, my - my daughter,
Mac, is, like, a huge fan.

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.631
And so, you know,
she woke us up the other night

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.066
when he dropped his single.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.401
-Dude.
-It woke us up.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.002
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.170
Like - we're like -

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.438
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.740
-At what time can you wake up
Woody Harrelson?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.275
Like, what - what's a good time?

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.777
-I don't think it's ever
a good idea.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.178
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.114
-Let a sleeping Woody lie?
-Exactly.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.415
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.884
-Now you - I should stress,
you needed a little sleep

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:01.420
because you did one of the great
late night endeavors.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.223
Last Saturday, you hosted "SNL"
for your fifth time.

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.559
-Yeah.
-Fantastic episode.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.661
-Yeah, that was -
that was exciting.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.730
-And I - let me say,
the five-Timers club --

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.233
the real accomplishment,
you didn't just knock out

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.801
five hosting stints
in seven years.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.203
You stretched this out.
-Yeah.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.472
-It speaks to the breadth
of your career.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.173
Your first one was 1989.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:23.976
Do you remember your first time
hosting "SNL"?

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.578
-Not even a little bit.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.713
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.047
-Well, hold - let me reframe it.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.315
Do you remember much
about last Saturday?

00:02:30.315 --> 00:02:31.851
-Nothing. Nothing at all.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:36.589
That's -- even then, I didn't --
I know that I left after --

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.992
-Yeah.
-After, at 6:00.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:39.992
-Yeah.

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:43.596
-So, that's where my memory
started.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.663
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:45.965
-Yeah.
-Amazing.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.668
-But is it - do you remember -
the high of hosting?

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.402
Does that feel the same,
even though you're doing it

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:51.704
for your fifth time?

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.707
-Oh, there was a serious high
of hosting going on.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.109
-I walked -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:59.412
-I promise I'm not trying
to walk right into this.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:04.116
-Everyone in the dressing room
had a whole high of hosting.

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:05.751
-So, you're saying
it's almost contagious

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:07.987
when they're around you.
-It was contagious.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.221
-Yeah.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.391
Thick with -- anyway.

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.092
-Hey, this is very exciting.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:16.462
So, you have your own --
your own weed dispensary?

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.297
-I do.
-Congratulations.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.166
-Yeah, yeah.
-The Woods?

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.835
-The Woods.
-And this is an L.A. billboard,

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.538
and this is an old photo of you.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.240
-Yeah.
-Now, I was thinking, like,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.442
what do you think this young man
would think if you told him

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:32.411
in the future,
you're going to own

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:35.348
a legal marijuana dispensary?

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.416
-Well, at the time,
he didn't smoke.

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:38.484
-Really?

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.319
-So, he would have been like,
"No way."

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.789
I was very religious
at that time.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:47.659
This is -- I was working as
a lifeguard at a --

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:52.298
anyway, someone sent this to --
it was at a church camp.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.666
I didn't want to get into
all that.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.569
But okay.
So, I used to go to church.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.504
Anyway, yeah.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.840
So, someone sent that to
The Woods.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.776
-Yeah.
-And then we were like,

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.078
"Well, let's just use this."
-Yeah.

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.847
I will say, yeah -- I mean,
I would have definitely guessed

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.683
"weed" before
"church camp lifeguard."

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.917
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:14.020
Based on the photo.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.155
Well, that's very exciting.
Have you enjoyed it?

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.824
I mean, it must be a nice moment
to be able to --

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:21.694
I mean, this is something you've
been a fan of for a while.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.163
-Well, it's really
the most beautiful place

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.231
you've ever seen.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.933
I mean,
it is stunningly beautiful.

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:32.037
Thomas Schoos, who is a partner,
did the designing,

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:34.773
and he's, like --
he's a brilliant designer.

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:37.109
So, it's, like --
it's beautiful.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.411
It's the most beautiful
dispensary in the world.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.246
After that,
I can't promise anything.

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:45.084
But there is - there's
a ganja giggle garden out back

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:48.321
where you can go out there
and, um, giggle.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.354
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.354 --> 00:04:51.357
-It's a giggle garden.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:52.825
This was amazing.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:56.162
Somebody -- in our lives, every
now and then, we might encounter

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:59.265
who we or other people will say
is your doppelganger.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.500
Right? You lay eyes on them
and you go, "Oh, my God,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.603
I can't believe I lived my whole
life and there's a person

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:04.737
on earth who looks
just like me."

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:05.738
-I can't wait to see this.
-Well, this is --

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.374
somebody posted this on Twitter.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.475
You responded to it.

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.843
Their daughter --
their infant daughter.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.845
-Oh, yes, yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.414
-And I was like, "How can an
infant daughter look like

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:16.682
Woody Harrelson?"
-Spitting image.

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:18.250
-I mean, that's insane.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.254
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.660
-What a trip.
-Yeah.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.562
I mean, can you imagine
how messed up

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:31.964
she's going to be in life?

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.165
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:35.134
Later, people are showing her
this picture.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.036
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.537
-I think she'll be --
I think she's gonna --

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:41.407
They say all babies grow out
of their Woody phase, yeah.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.775
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.143
-I've got a lot more questions,
including about the film.

00:05:45.143 --> 00:05:47.580
We'll be right back with more
from Woody Harrelson.

